# Same-origin: the SPA is served by the same ASP.NET host that serves /api, so a
# relative base needs no CORS entry and no certificate of its own. An absolute
# URL here is baked into the bundle at build time and would send every browser to
# its own machine instead of the server.
#
# Deployed as an IIS Application named "ehr", so every URL the browser sees is
# prefixed with /ehr. Both values below must carry that prefix and must be kept
# in step with the application alias in IIS -- the paths are baked into the
# bundle at build time, so changing the alias means rebuilding, not just
# reconfiguring. (The IIS *site* name is not part of the URL; only the
# application alias is.)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/ehr/api
VITE_APP_BASE_URL=/ehr/
VITE_USE_MOCK=false
